@* No-JS friendly formatting help. Native <details> — works with JavaScript off.
   Documents the markdown link syntax so anchor text can be set without the toolbar. *@
<details class="fmt-help">
    <summary>Formatting &amp; links</summary>
    <div class="fmt-help-body">
        <p style="margin:0 0 6px;"><strong>Link with your own wording</strong> &mdash; put the text in <code>[&nbsp;]</code> and the web address in <code>(&nbsp;)</code>:</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 8px;"><code>[Monero project](https://getmonero.org)</code> &nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp; <a href="https://getmonero.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Monero project</a></p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 6px;"><strong>Embed a YouTube video</strong> &mdash; put a YouTube link on its own line (or use the ▶ YouTube button). It becomes a click-to-play video; nothing loads until a reader clicks, so it still works on Tor/VPN.</p>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0;">Also: <code>**bold**</code>, <code>*italic*</code>, <code>&gt;&nbsp;quote</code>, <code>`code`</code>. With JavaScript on, highlight text and click the 🔗 toolbar button.</p>
    </div>
</details>
